# propellant_box.k26asm - a calibration article that spends what it
# thrusts.
#
# WHAT THIS IS. A shape, not a craft. Nothing here is a claim about
# any vehicle: the masses, the dimensions and the thruster layout are
# chosen so that every quantity in the propulsion model has a closed
# form a reader can check by hand, and so that each of them moves.
#
# The hull is a cube of half extent one metre carrying a tonne. The
# tank is a smaller cube of four hundred kilograms held a metre and a
# quarter off the hull's centre along the y axis, which is what makes
# the article worth having: the vehicle's centre of mass sits at
# 1.25 * m / (1000 + m) along y with m the propellant left, so it
# travels from 0.357 m at a full tank to the hull's own centre at an
# empty one, and every thruster torque, which is taken about the
# centre of mass, travels with it.
#
# The two thrusters differ in specific impulse by a factor of four,
# which is about the spread between a storable bipropellant main
# engine and a cold gas attitude thruster. `main` thrusts along the
# body x axis from behind, and `vernier` thrusts along z from a point
# on the x axis, so the second turns the article about two axes while
# the first pushes it along one. A craft whose thrusters all shared a
# specific impulse could not tell a per-thruster model from a
# per-vehicle one, which is the reason for the spread.
#
# The specific impulses are of the right order for the two engine
# classes named above and are not read from any source: 300 s for a
# storable bipropellant engine and 75 s for cold gas. Nothing is cited
# here because nothing here is a real article.

assembly propellant_box
    frame x_to_port

    provenance mass "calibration shape, not a craft: a tonne of hull chosen for round arithmetic" computed
    provenance tank "a chosen tank placement, held off the hull's centre so the centre of mass travels as it empties; this is an arrangement and not a measurement" modelled
    provenance isp "chosen figures of the right order for a storable bipropellant engine and for cold gas; no source is cited because no article is claimed" modelled
    provenance thrust "chosen so that a full tank is worth about 850 m/s and empties in about an hour at the main engine's full throttle" modelled

    component hull
        mass 1000.0
        at 0.0 0.0 0.0
        collider box 1.0 1.0 1.0
    end

    component tank
        mass 400.0
        at 0.0 1.25 0.0
        collider box 0.4 0.4 0.4
        propellant
    end

    thruster main
        at -1.0 0.0 0.0
        dir 1.0 0.0 0.0
        thrust 400.0
        isp_s 300.0
    end

    thruster vernier
        at 1.0 0.0 0.0
        dir 0.0 0.0 1.0
        thrust 50.0
        isp_s 75.0
    end
end
